  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Figshare dataset has begun to register scholarly uptake: OpenAlex records 1 citation, and the reuse graph shows 2 documented downstream reuses, including a linked associated article. The record is still early and sparse, but it already shows the dataset being incorporated into follow-on research.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in 2023 as an open-access dataset on Figshare, this CellMap Project resource provides near-isotropic reconstructed FIB-SEM volume electron microscopy of P7 mouse pancreas. Its impact record is modest but real: the dataset has 1 citation in OpenAlex, and the data-citation and reuse records show that it has been directly referenced in a preprint and reused in two downstream outputs overall, including an associated article. That pattern suggests the dataset is being used as a research resource rather than remaining only a deposited file.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest signal comes from a follow-on preprint on beta cell primary cilia, which cites the dataset and places it within a research context spanning cell biology and pancreatic function and diabetes. The cited work draws on contributors from multiple countries and institutions, indicating that the dataset is supporting collaborative analysis beyond the original team. At the same time, the citation base is still small, so the record supports an early-stage uptake story rather than a broad diffusion claim.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Repository and access metadata point to straightforward discoverability and preservation: the dataset is openly available through Figshare, indexed in OpenAIRE, and connected to a prior version and a related article through DataCite links. Datacite reports 0 views and 0 downloads, so there is no usage evidence from that source to add to the scholarly signals already observed.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the evidence shows a niche but meaningful start to reuse in specialized biomedical imaging and pancreas research. The impact footprint is presently defined more by concrete downstream scholarly use than by public attention, and the available record remains too limited to support stronger claims about reach or standing.</p>",
